#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail

source "$(dirname "$0")/lib/mise.bash"
ensure_tools

VERSION="$(buildkite-agent meta-data get release-version)"
TAG="$VERSION"
# package-and-push-chart recorded the commit the build started from. No release
# step writes a commit to `main`, so the tag names the commit that was built.
RELEASE_COMMIT="$(buildkite-agent meta-data get release-commit)"
CONTROL_PLANE_IMAGE="ghcr.io/zhming0/dsh-yawn-control-plane"
RUNNER_IMAGE="ghcr.io/zhming0/dsh-yawn-runner"

echo "+++ :github: Creating GitHub release"
# --target creates the tag at the commit the build started from, which is what
# the images and the chart were built and published from.
gh release create "$TAG" --target "$RELEASE_COMMIT" --title "$TAG" --generate-notes --notes "## Images

\`\`\`
docker pull ${CONTROL_PLANE_IMAGE}:${VERSION}
docker pull ${RUNNER_IMAGE}:${VERSION}
\`\`\`

Both built for \`linux/amd64\` and \`linux/arm64\`. The control-plane image is the dsh
distribution: dsh with the web profile and this control plane assembled at the same
version. The control plane inside it defaults to the runner image tag above, so the
pair always ships together.

## Sandbox pool

The pool base names the runner image without a tag. An overlay pins it to this
release:

\`\`\`yaml
images:
  - name: ${RUNNER_IMAGE}
    newTag: ${VERSION}
\`\`\`

Use this version for the \`ref\` of the base too, so the manifests and the image
are the same release: https://github.com/zhming0/dsh-yawn/blob/${TAG}/docs/runners/kubernetes.md
"
